        "datasetLabel": "Banking",
        "industry": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "why": "sheet.sources must be an array of {industry, dataset, label} entries, never a bare string; a string here is the same DE-021 shape as source.industry-as-object, just on the fan-out list",
      "payload": "Banking"
    },
    {
      "why": "the record whitelist in Console.save_view (server.py ~:963) builds `value` from named keys only (id, name, saved_at, sourceKey, source, sheets, active); a top-level industry key outside `source` is silently DROPPED, so a producer that puts it there instead of inside `source` is wrong even though the request itself is not otherwise malformed",
